{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted → 63.9% acc), evidence is extremely sparse and the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality and fusion mechanism are actually contributing beyond the RNA signal. Config_003 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean ablation of config_001 that changes only the model setting (removing the image branch and fusion) while keeping the same RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation. If config_003 performs comparably to config_001, the image modality adds little value under these encoders and we should focus budget on RNA representation choices; if it performs substantially worse, the image is contributing meaningfully and we should explore image encoder and fusion variations. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the core multimodal design decision before committing further budget to more complex multimodal variants."
}

